      "content": "that makes sense. so basically the standard patient used for the ABCDE rules is just the baseline for most medical training, right? given that, if i'm looking at a patient from a minority group, are there specific physiological or biological differences in how their skin actually behaves, or is it mostly just about the lesion being harder to see against the background pigment?",
