      "content": "The ABCDE rules train clinicians to recognize suspicious lesions, but may not account for physiological differences in skin behavior among individuals from various ethnic backgrounds. While skin pigment density and type (e.g., melanin content) can affect visibility, melanoma presentation is equally related to cellular characteristics and immune responses. For darker skin tones, studies have identified specific melanoma risk factors, including a stronger association with duplex melanocytic lesions, higher rates of ulceration, and increased thickness. Additionally, darker skin-dependent imaging techniques, like dermoscopy, are being developed to improve melanoma detection in these populations.",
